---
import { SITE } from "../constants";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <blockquote>{SITE.description}</blockquote>
  <p>
    This library is not meant to be an all-in-one solution, but rather a
    sensible starting point for new projects.
  </p>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>One:</strong>
    This library is meant to fully embrace <em>cascading style sheets</em> instead
    of giving you a way around them. It styles semantic elements in a simple, consistent
    way, setting you up to be able to extend and/or override the defaults as your
    design requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Two:</strong> The fundamental philosophy of this project is to use ratios
    to setup consistent sizing and spacing. The default is to use the <em
      >golden ratio</em
    >, but through config you can set to other classic ratios.
  </p>
  <p>
    Importantly, as is the case with design, a system has been created then
    meaningful deviations have been embraced to fine-tune it to look and feel
    correct. Thus, you may notice that we don't 100% adhere to the selected
    ratio, but default to doing so.
  </p>
  <hr />
  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/demo`} class="button"
      >See demo &rarr;</a
    >
  </p>
  <hr />
  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero JavaScript</strong> — Pure CSS, no runtime overhead.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ratio-based scale</strong> — Typography, spacing, and line-heights all
      derived from a single configurable ratio (default: golden ratio φ ≈ 1.618).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatic dark mode</strong> — Respects <code
        >prefers-color-scheme</code
      >
      out of the box.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>CSS custom properties</strong> — Easy theming and runtime customization
      via variables like <code>--font-size-lg</code> and <code
        >--spacing-md</code
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Semantic element styling</strong> — Sensible defaults for headings,
      paragraphs, lists, tables, blockquotes, code, forms, and more.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Modular Sass architecture</strong> — Import only what you need via mixins
      like <code>aeraline-base</code>, <code>aeraline-headings</code>, or use <code
        >aeraline</code
      > for everything.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>12-column flexbox grid</strong> (Optional, opt-in) — Responsive grid
      with breakpoints at <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, and <code>lg</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Minimal utility classes</strong> — Spacing (<code>.mt-md</code>, <code
        >.p-lg</code
      >), typography (<code>.text-xl</code>, <code>.h3</code>), and flexbox
      helpers without the bloat.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Form &amp; button styling</strong> — Inputs, selects, textareas, and
      buttons styled consistently.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lightweight reset</strong> — Clean slate without nuking useful defaults.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
